# Copy to .env on the server you deploy to (never commit .env).
#
# On a lab machine the defaults are fine: state in ./data/jenkins_home, port 8082.
# On a server, keep the state OUTSIDE the checkout so a redeploy cannot touch it,
# and expose Jenkins on a port your reverse proxy can reach.
#
# JENKINS_HOME_DIR=/srv/jenkins/home
# JENKINS_PORT=8082
# JENKINS_AGENT_PORT=50001

# The state directory must be writable by uid 1000 (the container's jenkins user):
#   sudo mkdir -p /srv/jenkins/home && sudo chown -R 1000:1000 /srv/jenkins
